-- title:
--   U_q-eigenvalue times a_q(g) equals q at auxiliary level
-- statement:
--   Fix a positive integer $M$, a Dirichlet character $\varepsilon$ modulo $M$ with values in $\mathbb{C}$, and a weight-$2$ cusp form $g$ on $\Gamma_1(M)$ which is primitive for $\varepsilon$ in the sense of [`CuspForm.IsPrimitiveForm`](def/CuspForm_PrimitiveFormGamma1.html#L38): its $q$-expansion satisfies $a_1(g)=1$, the recursion $a_{pn}(g)+\varepsilon(p)p^{k-1}[p\mid n]a_{n/p}(g)=a_p(g)a_n(g)$ for primes $p\nmid M$, the multiplicativity $a_{\ell n}(g)=a_\ell(g)a_n(g)$ for primes $\ell\mid M$, and $g$ has nebentypus $\varepsilon$; moreover no proper divisor $M''\mid M$ carries a nonzero weight-$2$ form with some nebentypus whose eigenpacket agrees with that of $g$ outside a finite set of primes. Let $p$ be a prime and $M'$ a positive multiple of $M$ satisfying the predicates [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsAll`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L58) and [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondCommuteBar`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L54) at level $M'$ (Hecke input data along every prime for $X_1(M')$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with rational and base-changed diamond automorphisms for each $d$ coprime to $M'$, and commutativity of all Hecke and diamond generators). Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals, $\Omega$ a field that is a $\mathbb{Q}_p$-algebra, $R$ a commutative ring, $\mathrm{toC}\colon R\to\mathbb{C}$ an injective ring homomorphism, $\psi\colon R\to\Omega$ a ring homomorphism, and $b,e\colon\mathbb{N}\to R$ such that $\mathrm{toC}(b_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$ and $\mathrm{toC}(e_\ell)=\varepsilon(\ell)$ for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$. Let $q$ be a prime with $q\mid M$, $q^2\nmid M$, $q\mid\operatorname{cond}\varepsilon$ and $q^2\nmid M'$, and let $b_q\in R$ satisfy $\mathrm{toC}(b_q)=a_q(g)$. Give $J_1(M')$, the degree-zero divisor class group of the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field of $X_1(M')$, the Hecke-algebra module structure [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleOneBar`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L129). Then for every ring homomorphism $\Lambda$ from the rational Hecke algebra — the $\mathbb{Q}_p$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{Q}_p}(\mathbb{Q}_p\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p}T_pJ_1(M'))$ generated by the image of the Hecke representation — to $\Omega$ which is $\mathbb{Q}_p$-linear (it commutes with the structure maps from $\mathbb{Q}_p$) and satisfies $\Lambda(T_\ell)\,\psi(e_\ell)=\psi(b_\ell)$ and $\Lambda(\langle\ell\rangle)\,\psi(e_\ell)=1$ for all primes $\ell\nmid M'$ with $\ell\notin S$, one has $\Lambda(T_q)\cdot\psi(b_q)=q$ in $\Omega$.
--
--   Since $q$ divides $M'$, the operator $T_q$ occurring in the conclusion is the $U_q$-operator at $q$, and the identity $\Lambda(U_q)\,a_q(g)=q$ is the Atkin–Lehner–Li relation for a newform whose level is exactly divisible by $q$ with $q$ dividing the conductor of the nebentypus, transported to an arbitrary character of the rational Hecke algebra of $J_1(M')$ reading the eigenpacket of $g$ away from $M'$ and $S$. It is used in the construction of the $p$-adic Galois representation attached to $g$ at auxiliary level, in the step describing the action of inertia at $q$.
